  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14214505/assets/cad4c483d2678c63382c13d43e3377c0a471ff510bd6b86ea37dad3adb440d9a.png)\n\nThe function $p(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-5,3].$ The graph of ${p}^{′}(x)$, the derivative of $p(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the region between the graph and the $x$-axis is $9.$\n\nGiven that $p(3)=-4,$ what is the maximum value ${p}_{\\text{max}}$ of $p(x)$ on the interval $[-5,3]?$\n\n${p}_{\\text{max}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
